{"name":"Sweet Dreams","hex":"#eccee5","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sweet dreams","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Phrase","definitions":["Said to someone before they fall asleep, wishing them a good sleep."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sweet_dreams"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sweet Dreams (1981 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Sweet Dreams is a 1981 Italian comedy-drama film directed, written and starring Nanni Moretti.\nIt entered the 38th Venice International Film Festival, in which won the Special Jury Prize."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/ea/Sogni_d%27oro_%281981_Film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweet_Dreams_(1981_film)","wikidata":"Q3061723"},{"title":"Sweet Dreams (Are Made of This)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Sweet Dreams (Are Made of This)\" is a song by the British synth-pop duo Eurythmics. It was released in January 1983 by RCA Records as the fourth and final single from their second album, Sweet Dreams (Are Made of This) (1983). It was Eurythmics' breakthrough hit, establishing them worldwide. It reached number two on the UK singles chart in March 1983 and number one on the US Billboard Hot 100 six months later; it was the first Eurythmics single released in the US."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/00/Eurythmics_SDAMOT.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweet_Dreams_(Are_Made_of_This)","wikidata":"Q1587664"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/ea/Sogni_d%27oro_%281981_Film%29.jpg/250px-Sogni_d%27oro_%281981_Film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/ea/Sogni_d%27oro_%281981_Film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wik